# Custom domain support, prepared but not enabled.
#
# GitHub Pages reads a file called exactly `CNAME` (no extension) from the
# published site root. This file is named CNAME.example on purpose, so it is
# inert until a domain actually exists.
#
# To enable a custom domain:
#   1. Point the domain's DNS at GitHub Pages:
#        - apex domain:      A/AAAA records to GitHub's Pages IPs
#        - www subdomain:    CNAME to parishruthiganesh.github.io
#   2. Copy this file:  cp public/CNAME.example public/CNAME
#   3. Replace the contents with the bare hostname on a single line, e.g.
#        parishruthi.dev
#   4. Update `site` in astro.config.mjs to https://<that hostname>
#      (canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, the sitemap and the RSS feed all read
#      from that value, so missing this step is the usual cause of a custom
#      domain that "works" but still advertises the github.io URL).
#   5. Commit, merge to main, and enable "Enforce HTTPS" in
#      Settings → Pages once the certificate has been issued.
